  ('field-vole', 'Field Vole', 'Microtus agrestis', 'land-mammals', 'A small, short-tailed, grey-brown vole of rough grassland, hidden in runs through the grass; a key food for owls and kestrels.', 'Rough grassland, moorland and field margins', 'Year-round; look for grass runways'),
  ('wood-mouse', 'Wood Mouse', 'Apodemus sylvaticus', 'land-mammals', 'A large-eyed, big-eared, golden-brown mouse with a long tail, active at night in woodland, gardens and hedgerows.', 'Woodland, hedgerows, gardens and farmland', 'Year-round, after dark; try a torch near sheds and bird tables'),
  ('house-mouse', 'House Mouse', 'Mus musculus', 'land-mammals', 'A small, grey-brown mouse with a long tail that lives alongside people in buildings and farms.', 'Houses, farm buildings and warehouses', 'Year-round, after dark'),
  ('harvest-mouse', 'Harvest Mouse', 'Micromys minutus', 'land-mammals', 'Britain''s smallest rodent, a tiny golden-red mouse that climbs tall grass with a grasping tail and weaves ball-shaped nests.', 'Tall grassland, reedbeds and field margins', 'Late summer to autumn, when nests are easiest to spot'),
  ('yellow-necked-mouse', 'Yellow-necked Mouse', 'Apodemus flavicollis', 'land-mammals', 'A large-eyed mouse like a wood mouse but with a yellow collar across its chest; a good climber of woodland trees.', 'Mature broadleaf woodland', 'After dark; autumn is best'),
