  ('edible-dormouse', 'Edible Dormouse', 'Glis glis', 'land-mammals', 'A large, grey, squirrel-like dormouse introduced near Tring in 1902; nocturnal, with a bushy tail, and sometimes found in lofts.', 'Woodland and buildings in the Chilterns', 'After dark, from late spring to autumn'),
